[ar:aarav_kharade1234]
[ti:I remember the wrong day]
[al:Bringing the world back]

[00:01.80]I remember the morning,
[00:06.12]The light across the floor,
[00:10.87]A blue sky through the window,
[00:16.16]And nothing more.
[00:29.89]I remember coffee cooling,
[00:32.89]Someone laughing down the hall,
[00:35.27]I remember summer breathing
[00:37.11]Through the curtains on the wall.
[00:40.57]There was music from the kitchen,
[00:42.67]There was sunlight in the street,
[00:45.18]I remember someone walking
[00:46.85]Barefoot beside me.
[00:50.29]It rained that morning.
[00:54.03]No...
[00:56.67]I remember the sun.
[01:07.58]I remember rain against the window,
[01:11.18]Silver running down the glass,
[01:13.04]I remember staying inside
[01:15.67]And watching hours slowly pass.
[01:17.93]There was a song beneath the thunder,
[01:20.51]Something soft I can't recall,
[01:22.60]I remember you were singing...
[01:24.98]There wasn't any music.
[01:28.15]Was the sky blue?
[01:30.18]Was the sky grey?
[01:32.87]Did I wake up?
[01:35.26]Did I dream the day?
[01:37.60]I remember the wrong day,
[01:40.16]I remember it so clear,
[01:42.37]I can see the shape of everything,
[01:44.84]I just can't make it real.
[01:47.59]I remember your voice,
[01:49.48]I remember your face,
[01:50.22]But every time I reach for you,
[01:51.27]The memory changes place.
[01:57.47]Was I there?
[01:59.72]Were you there?
[02:02.05]Did it happen?
[02:05.94]Did I care?
[02:07.74]I remember the wrong day,
[02:11.82]And I don't know what is true.
[02:17.41]I remember yellow walls,
[02:19.60]No, they were white.
[02:20.20]I remember leaving
[02:21.09]Before midnight.
[02:22.49]I remember your jacket,
[02:24.09]I remember the door,
[02:25.03]I remember saying,
[02:26.05]“I've been here before.”
[02:27.67]But the room was never yellow.
[02:29.11]There was never any door.
[02:30.17]And the person I remember
[02:31.35]Had never met me before.
[02:33.04]So who was I remembering?
[02:37.25]What color was the sky?
[02:41.50]I don't know.
[02:42.11]What song was playing?
[02:43.43]I don't know.
[02:46.30]What did the room smell like?
[02:48.16]I don't know.
[02:48.71]What did you say to me?
[02:51.12]I don't know.
[02:51.74]I don't remember the day.
[02:53.19]I remember remembering it.
[02:59.53]Maybe the rain was sunlight,
[03:01.18]Maybe silence sounded like a song,
[03:03.28]Maybe you were never with me,
[03:05.61]Maybe I've been wrong all along.
[03:08.59]Maybe every time I told it,
[03:10.86]I changed another piece,
[03:13.28]Until the story became something
[03:16.05]That was easier to keep.
[03:18.77]I remember the wrong day,
[03:21.05]I remember every lie,
[03:23.70]Every color, every shadow,
[03:25.21]Every version in my mind.
[03:26.80]I remember your voice,
[03:28.05]Though I don't know if it was you,
[03:31.20]I remember what I lost,
[03:33.91]Though I don't know if I ever knew.
[03:36.64]Was I there?
[03:38.00]Were you there?
[03:39.34]Was it real?
[03:41.98]Was it fear?
[03:44.14]I remember the wrong day,
[03:47.95]And the day remembers me.
[03:58.94]I remember the morning...
[04:00.93]No.
[04:01.84]I remember the rain...
[04:03.82]No.
[04:09.46]There was music...
[04:11.15]No.
[04:16.63]You were there...
[04:18.98]No.
[04:22.48]Maybe it never happened that way.
[04:27.28]Maybe that's how I remember it.
[04:41.18]I remember...